# The district's Google Calendar, in iCal format. The calendar page reads it on
# the server and refreshes hourly; without it the page shows the events
# recorded in lib/events.ts.
#
# Google Calendar → Settings → (the district calendar) → Integrate calendar →
# "Secret address in iCal format". The calendar stays private; treat this
# address like a password: never committed or shared. If it leaks, click
# "Reset" next to it and update both copies below.
# Fallback if a Workspace admin has disabled secret addresses: make the
# calendar public and use its "Public address in iCal format" instead.
#
# It is kept in two places:
# 1. Runtime: a secret on the Cloudflare Worker (`npx wrangler secret put
#    DISTRICT_CALENDAR_ICS_URL`, or the dashboard). The hourly refresh reads it.
# 2. Build time: a file named `.env.build` in the project root (git-ignored),
#    holding the line below. `npm run deploy` / `preview` / `upload` load it
#    into the build's environment only (`npm run cf-build`), so each deploy
#    prerenders the live calendar instead of the recorded events.
#
# Do NOT put it in `.env`, `.env.local` or `.env.production*`: the OpenNext
# adapter copies those files into the deployed Worker's code.
DISTRICT_CALENDAR_ICS_URL=
